# Watch contract and deletion boundaries

Bellwether controls Herdr and observes agent state or pane output. It does not own workflow claims, leases, or completion decisions.

## Keep

- The existing XState lifecycle: starting → running → matched, timedOut, targetGone, failed, or cancelled.
- Exact socket cancellation, dead-agent probes, bounded terminal receipts, and session-generation wake suppression.
- Guarded pane close. Both the tool and slash command refuse the pane hosting Pi. Closing a pane is not a graceful agent stop.

## Delete

- The unused workflow-watch adapter types. No in-repo caller or workflow result contract justified them.
- The separate `wakeSent` flag. `finishWatch` changes status before invoking callbacks, so its terminal guard already prevents a second wake.
- The duplicated optional watch-input fields and unused actor-input generation. Reuse the two typed start variants; keep generation only on the registry record that checks it.

## Agent-facing receipts

`watchReceiptText` in `src/watch.ts` formats start/status/cancel results and background wakes. It exposes observed agent state and identity, failure codes, or up to 12 lines / 2 KiB of terminal evidence. Prefer the matched line over unrelated terminal history. Strip ANSI controls, mark truncation, and keep terminal text explicitly untrusted. Structured receipts remain intact in `details`.

The public `list` action returns active watches by default. `history: true` includes retained terminal receipts; status-by-ID still works after settlement. This removes routine history output without changing lifecycle, retention, cancellation, or wake delivery.

## Wake delivery

`src/wake-record.ts` encodes settled watches and degraded ping waits as `sh.mschf.agentgraph.wake` records. Bellwether sends them to the owner's live Rat King name. pi-ratking owns urgency, batching, withdrawal, and delivery through pi-until. Bellwether no longer holds wakes behind the current agent run.

The record omits socket routing. Text is capped at 8192 characters, terminal evidence at 12 lines / 2048 characters, and encoded JSON at 16 KB. No live self name means one local follow-up. Refused mail or a missing delivery result after 15 seconds adds a warning and delivers the same local follow-up.

Cancel sends a `cancelled` record for a mailed wake, including when the original send is still in flight. Owner pane close uses the same withdrawal path. Local follow-ups cannot be withdrawn. Notify, silent, and already-reported receipts stay local only.

## Evidence

`src/watch.test.ts` checks required variant fields, one terminal notification, cancellation, generation isolation, shutdown, and receipt limits. `src/watch-receipt.test.ts` checks evidence selection, UTF-8/line bounds, truncation, and failure codes. `src/pi-bellwether.test.ts` checks that status and wake expose the same evidence, terminal history is opt-in, and wake mail and cancellation reach the event bus. `src/wake-record.test.ts` checks strict field limits, clipping, fallback deadlines, and withdrawal ordering. Dropping the cancellation send must fail both the unit withdrawal test and the extension cancellation test.
